# .mill/agents — per-project tier → (agent, model) mapping.
#
# Same shape as .mill/gauntlet and .mill/role-capabilities: plain bash,
# sourced by the coordinator's dispatch procedure (see
# .claude/skills/delegate/SKILL.md, section 2). Each tier declares the
# agent binary and the model identifier the worker's terminal starts with:
#
#   orca terminal create --command "<agent> --model <model>"
#
# The tier comes from the role's ROLE.md frontmatter `model:` field:
#   free→paid  producing roles — dispatched on free first, re-dispatched on
#              paid when the cheap attempt fails on judgment rather than on
#              execution
#   pro        judging roles — dispatched straight onto pro, no free attempt
#
# Measured free models, from `opencode models`, so nobody has to rediscover
# them:
#   opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free
#   opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash
#   ...and others suffixed -free
#
# Copy this file to .mill/agents and set the models your provider offers.
# .mill/agents is per-project and gitignored; this example stays tracked.
# The agent can be anything `orca terminal create --command` accepts — omp,
# pi, command-code, claude.

free_agent="omp"
free_model="opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash"

paid_agent="omp"
paid_model="opencode/deepseek-v4-pro"

pro_agent="omp"
pro_model="opencode/claude-opus-4-5"
